WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.787
Every flat shape has sides and corners.
Count them, and you can name it.

2
00:00:10.007 --> 00:00:14.976
Solid shapes have faces and edges.
Shapes fold, and shapes turn.

3
00:00:15.476 --> 00:00:18.773
Here is a triangle. A
side is one straight edge.

4
00:00:18.993 --> 00:00:23.126
Go round in order, and count
each side once: one, two, three.

5
00:00:23.346 --> 00:00:26.133
A corner is the point
where two sides meet.

6
00:00:26.353 --> 00:00:30.393
Count the corners the same way,
going round: one, two, three.

7
00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:34.653
Now try a bigger shape. Count
round the pentagon: five sides.

8
00:00:34.873 --> 00:00:38.542
It has five corners too.
Every side ends at a corner.

9
00:00:39.042 --> 00:00:41.829
Counting the sides tells
you the shape's name.

10
00:00:42.049 --> 00:00:47.157
Three sides make a triangle. Four
make a square or a rectangle.

11
00:00:47.377 --> 00:00:51.324
Five sides make a pentagon.
Six sides make a hexagon.

12
00:00:51.544 --> 00:00:56.467
A shape turned round is still the same
shape. A tipped square is still a square.

13
00:00:56.967 --> 00:01:02.493
A face is a flat part you could paint.
Every face of a cube is a square.

14
00:01:02.713 --> 00:01:07.729
Count the faces of the cube:
one, two, three, four, five, six.

15
00:01:07.949 --> 00:01:12.082
The line where two faces meet
is an edge. A cube has twelve.

16
00:01:12.302 --> 00:01:16.203
A cube has eight corners
as well. A dice is a cube.

17
00:01:16.423 --> 00:01:21.299
A tin of beans is a cylinder. A
ball is a sphere, curved all over.

18
00:01:21.519 --> 00:01:27.789
A door is a flat shape: a rectangle. A
clock face is a flat shape: a circle.

19
00:01:28.289 --> 00:01:32.979
A line of symmetry is a fold
line. Both halves match exactly.

20
00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:36.868
Fold this square down the middle.
The halves land on each other.

21
00:01:37.088 --> 00:01:41.082
A rectangle folds across the
middle as well. That works too.

22
00:01:41.302 --> 00:01:45.853
A slanted fold does not work. The
halves are not the same shape.

23
00:01:46.353 --> 00:01:50.021
A turn can be a quarter turn,
a half turn or a whole turn.

24
00:01:50.241 --> 00:01:53.678
Clockwise means the way the
hands of a clock go round.

25
00:01:53.898 --> 00:01:57.520
This arrow points up. Turn
it a quarter turn clockwise.

26
00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:01.920
Now it points right. Another
quarter, and it points down.

27
00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.877
Two quarter turns make a half turn.
A whole turn comes back to the start.

28
00:02:07.097 --> 00:02:11.973
Anticlockwise is the other way round.
A quarter turn from up points left.

29
00:02:12.473 --> 00:02:17.070
Turn a square slowly all the way
round. It looks the same four times.

30
00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.517
One for each equal corner. Count
the last one, back at the start.

31
00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:25.732
Count the sides and the corners.
The numbers always match.

32
00:02:25.952 --> 00:02:29.528
Count its sides to name
it: three, four, five, six.

33
00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:33.834
Solid shapes have faces, edges
and corners you can count.

34
00:02:34.054 --> 00:02:39.488
A fold line makes matching halves. A
whole turn comes back to the start.
